  "id": "renshaw-cell",
  "term": "Renshaw cell",
  "definition": "A Renshaw cell is an inhibitory interneuron in the ventral gray horn of the spinal cord. It forms a reciprocal connection with a motor neuron, receiving input from that neuron and sending inhibitory signals back to it.",
